description:
Design a toggle flip-flop (TFF) that changes its output state on the rising edge of the clock signal when the T input is high. The output Q is reset to a low state when the reset signal (rst) is low. If T is low, the output remains unchanged. This module is used to create a circuit element that toggles between two states based on clock pulses, enabling memory storage of binary states.
module top_module(
	input T, clk, rst,
	output reg Q
);

code:
module top_module(
	input T, clk, rst,
	output reg Q
);always @ (posedge clk, negedge rst)
		if (!rst) Q <= 0;
		else case (T)
			1'b0 : Q <= Q;
			1'b1 : Q <= !Q;
		endcase

endmodule

