description:
Design a 3-to-8 decoder that translates a 3-bit input into one of eight outputs. The module has an enable signal that, when low, forces all outputs to zero. When the enable signal is high, the decoder activates one specific output corresponding to the binary value of the input, setting that output to high while all other outputs remain low. This design is useful for applications requiring address decoding or signal routing in digital systems.
module top_module(
    input [2:0] in,
    input enable,
    output reg [7:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [2:0] in,
    input enable,
    output reg [7:0] out
);always @ (in or enable) begin
        if (enable == 1'b0) begin
            out <= 8'b0;
        end else begin
            case (in)
                3'b000: out <= 8'b00000001;
                3'b001: out <= 8'b00000010;
                3'b010: out <= 8'b00000100;
                3'b011: out <= 8'b00001000;
                3'b100: out <= 8'b00010000;
                3'b101: out <= 8'b00100000;
                3'b110: out <= 8'b01000000;
                3'b111: out <= 8'b10000000;
                default: out <= 8'b0;
            endcase
        end
    end

endmodule

