Design a circuit that functions as a configurable adder. It takes a 4-bit input and, when the enable signal is high, adds the value '2' (binary 010) to the input data, producing a 3-bit wide output. If the enable signal is not asserted, the output directly reflects the input value. The module operates on the rising edge of a clock signal.
